# Persian (فارسی) translation catalog for the Foolad Tabar Workflow platform
# CHROME (sidebar, tabs, buttons, field labels, status/state labels, page
# titles) — never for CONTENT (a company's own name, a person's own comment,
# report or reminder text, or anything else someone typed), which is never
# run through this catalog regardless of the strings below.
#
# This file is normally generated and kept up to date with
#     python manage.py makemessages -l fa
# (add the new `{% trans %}` / `{% blocktrans %}` strings first, then run it)
# and compiled with
#     python manage.py compilemessages
# Both of those shell out to the real GNU gettext tools (xgettext / msguniq /
# msgfmt respectively) via Python's `django.core.management.utils.popen_wrapper`
# — Django does not reimplement either. On the machine this catalog was first
# built on, only the gettext *runtime* (gettext.exe, used by Python's own
# stdlib `gettext` module to READ a compiled .mo at request time — which is
# all this app needs to actually serve translations) was on PATH; the
# developer toolchain (msgfmt/msguniq/xgettext, used only to BUILD/rebuild a
# catalog) was not installed, so neither management command could run there.
# This one entry (the Settings page's "Language" card heading — this round's
# single smoke-test string, see accounts/templates/accounts/settings.html)
# was therefore added and compiled to django.mo by hand instead, as the
# stopgap the task explicitly allows for. The Dockerfile now installs the
# `gettext` apt package (see its own comment) specifically so the real
# commands above work wherever this image is built, for every string later
# stages add — this hand-editing step is not meant to be how the catalog is
# maintained going forward.
#
