# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AUDIT #134 FOLLOW-UP — impersonation: admin can now "Log in as" a General
# Manager.
#
# accounts/views.py::impersonate_start used to refuse a General Manager as an
# impersonation TARGET together with a Platform Administrator, both under one
# shared refusal message: "Administrator and General Manager accounts cannot
# be impersonated." The owner asked for a Platform Administrator to be able
# to log in as ANY person regardless of role, including the General Manager,
# so that check now excludes Administrator only — the old combined message
# would have been actively wrong for a General Manager target once that
# exclusion no longer applies to them, so it is replaced with a narrower one
# naming Administrator alone. The old msgid above (search this file for
# "Administrator and General Manager accounts cannot be impersonated.") is no
# longer referenced by any .py/.html file as of this change; left in this
# catalog unused rather than deleted, same as every other retired string here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

